WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:05.200
- All right, Rocco.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:06.033
- Yes.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.380
- Rocco, where are you from
originally? Where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:09.223
- I grew up in Los Vegas.

00:00:09.223 --> 00:00:10.056
- Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:10.056 --> 00:00:12.187
Did you grow up with both of your parents?

00:00:12.187 --> 00:00:13.160
(sighs) My mom.

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.441
I grew up with my mom

00:00:14.441 --> 00:00:17.470
and my step-dad.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:18.303
He raised me.

00:00:18.303 --> 00:00:20.840
My biological dad was in
prison for most of my life.

00:00:23.242 --> 00:00:25.670
He was that motorcycle cat.

00:00:25.670 --> 00:00:26.503
You know?

00:00:26.503 --> 00:00:27.336
Motorcycle club.

00:00:28.469 --> 00:00:30.840
He got busted for selling cris,

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.310
crystal method,

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:33.623
methamphetamines,

00:00:35.539 --> 00:00:36.372
and he went away yeah,

00:00:36.372 --> 00:00:37.890
for most of my life he was gone.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:39.480
But my step-dad that raised me,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.530
is just aces, dude

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.633
I felt really, really
blessed to have him as a dad.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.490
- And how was your childhood otherwise?

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.795
Just, any abuse? Any craziness?

00:00:49.795 --> 00:00:51.393
- (chuckles) Yeah to be honest,

00:00:51.393 --> 00:00:52.226
yeah there was.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:54.880
I'm surprised I'm talking about it but,

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.760
there was a really nasty, demented,

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:00.168
just fucking twisted neighbor who,

00:01:00.168 --> 00:01:01.947
(strumming guitar idly)

00:01:01.947 --> 00:01:03.000
I mean you can probably gather,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:03.833
but, he like,

00:01:03.833 --> 00:01:04.740
the whole sexual

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:10.300
just abuse and disgusting-ness,

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:14.173
that around like four to like seven.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.010
Yeah. So anyway.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:18.843
Other than that, I mean

00:01:18.843 --> 00:01:19.996
I feel like I had a

00:01:19.996 --> 00:01:20.829
(clears throat)

00:01:20.829 --> 00:01:21.728
Excuse me.

00:01:21.728 --> 00:01:22.823
I had a good childhood.

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:24.833
Generally happy kid.

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.263
Yeah I mean, I felt
blessed growing up still.

00:01:30.263 --> 00:01:31.096
Know what I mean?

00:01:31.096 --> 00:01:33.030
I was a little fat

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.597
and yeah I'm not so fat now I guess.

00:01:36.597 --> 00:01:38.210
Yeah, I don't know.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:40.473
- So, you left home at what age?

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.440
- When I was seventeen.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.720
Yeah, I gotta--
What's that?

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:45.607
- Where'd you go?

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.230
- I moved into an apartment

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.737
with my girlfriend at the time.

00:01:49.737 --> 00:01:50.570
Know what I mean?

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:51.403
Just stopped.

00:01:51.403 --> 00:01:52.490
I wanted to get out of the
house as soon as possible.

00:01:52.490 --> 00:01:53.323
Like do my own thing.

00:01:53.323 --> 00:01:54.156
I started working

00:01:54.156 --> 00:01:54.989
for the department of transportation

00:01:54.989 --> 00:01:57.000
which was what my mom
was doing at the time.

00:01:59.228 --> 00:02:00.061
And, yeah I did that.

00:02:00.061 --> 00:02:01.750
I worked in the sign shop there.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:02.950
Actually ran into,

00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.610
when you're first working there,

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:06.640
you're on probation.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.240
And I ran into the like,

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:12.200
the head Department of
Transportation guy's car

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.230
with a state vehicle.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:15.110
And so I was fired like,

00:02:15.110 --> 00:02:16.000
immediately.
(snaps fingers)

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.630
But it was a good job, you know,

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:19.243
for the first couple months I was there.

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.170
- And then you came to LA at what point?

00:02:24.020 --> 00:02:26.700
- (sighs) It was Father's Day 2006.

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:29.070
I got hired to play bass for this girl

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:32.093
who was signed to Virgin UK Records.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.694
And I just dropped
everything and came out.

00:02:35.694 --> 00:02:36.527
You know?

00:02:36.527 --> 00:02:37.360
I was stoked.

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.280
I played music for freaking ever

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.520
and the opportunity to
come to LA from Vegas is,

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.240
I'm not gonna pass that up, you know?

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:46.940
So, I dropped everything and came out.

00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:48.683
And been here ever since.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:51.273
- So now you're living where?

00:02:51.273 --> 00:02:52.590
On Skid Row?

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.800
not on the row but

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:55.863
I like in a hatch.

00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:59.820
It's like what most people don't know,

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.300
but in LA,

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:03.150
I don't know about the
rest of the country but,

00:03:03.150 --> 00:03:05.770
in LA on the freeways,

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:07.880
the underpasses were like you can,

00:03:07.880 --> 00:03:09.580
just an underpass,

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:10.640
the bridge is at,

00:03:10.640 --> 00:03:12.450
if you walk up along side there

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.970
to the belly of the bridge,

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:15.750
there's like little hatches inside there.

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.230
And if you go,

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:18.860
there's one over on,

00:03:18.860 --> 00:03:19.970
I'll tell you exactly where.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:22.030
Over on Figueroa and Temple.

00:03:22.030 --> 00:03:23.430
I stay in one of those hatches.

00:03:23.430 --> 00:03:24.530
There's four under the bridge right there,

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:25.920
and you jump up inside there.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.520
I don't know what it's used for.

00:03:28.699 --> 00:03:29.532
Like, I don't have a clue.

00:03:29.532 --> 00:03:31.100
It's like the size of,

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.050
I don't even know how to describe it.

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:32.940
Like maybe,

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.773
40 by like

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.230
20 feet?

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.410
It's huge. It's huge.

00:03:39.410 --> 00:03:41.890
It's maybe like five,

00:03:41.890 --> 00:03:44.070
10 tall, the height.

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.570
And a bunch of us live there.

00:03:45.570 --> 00:03:46.510
A whole mess of us

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:48.120
in the hatches, yeah.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:48.953
It's not bad.

00:03:48.953 --> 00:03:50.180
I mean, it's better than being,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:51.600
to me it's better than being in a tent.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:53.240
It feels very less exposed.

00:03:53.240 --> 00:03:56.220
But the California Highway Patrol comes by

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.070
and messes with us

00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:00.600
and has us do little weird
sobriety testings for them.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.713
Which is just random but,

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:04.493
I mean yeah.

00:04:04.493 --> 00:04:05.620
I kinda like being out here

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:07.020
for a minute on the streets.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:10.234
That felt like an upgrade honestly.

00:04:10.234 --> 00:04:11.233
The hatch is better.

00:04:11.233 --> 00:04:12.550
- Yes, it's probably safer right?

00:04:12.550 --> 00:04:14.210
- Yeah it feels safer for sure.

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:15.043
Absolutely.

00:04:15.043 --> 00:04:15.876
Absolutely feels safer, yeah.

00:04:15.876 --> 00:04:17.763
- And so what is your drug now?

00:04:17.763 --> 00:04:18.596
- Heroin.

00:04:18.596 --> 00:04:19.520
Heroin and crystal.

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:21.736
- When did that start?

00:04:21.736 --> 00:04:22.569
- When did it start?

00:04:22.569 --> 00:04:23.943
- Yeah?

00:04:23.943 --> 00:04:25.280
- (sighs) Heroin specifically?

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.510
- Well, drugs in general I guess?

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.343
- Drugs I guess,

00:04:28.343 --> 00:04:29.660
I was 14.

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:31.960
Yeah, I mean like the gradual progression

00:04:31.960 --> 00:04:33.360
as I feel like most cats do,

00:04:34.310 --> 00:04:35.290
like weed,

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:38.640
then there's mushrooms,

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.800
coke (chuckles)

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:41.633
then pills.

00:04:41.633 --> 00:04:43.710
Honestly when I found painkillers

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:45.880
that was like putting on
new skin for me, dude.

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:46.713
I felt like

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.770
comfortable for the first time ever.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:50.603
I don't know why

00:04:50.603 --> 00:04:52.760
but I've always felt
uncomfortable in my skin.

00:04:52.760 --> 00:04:54.150
And painkillers for me for some reason,

00:04:54.150 --> 00:04:56.024
the second I took it, dude the second.

00:04:56.024 --> 00:04:56.857
The first freaking pill was like

00:04:56.857 --> 00:04:57.690
(snaps fingers)

00:04:57.690 --> 00:04:58.726
That's what I need
(snaps fingers)

00:04:58.726 --> 00:05:01.800
That's the jam that makes me feel okay.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.240
Now my goal is in life is
just to stay high basically.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.200
And I know that's depressing thinking

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:09.670
of that but I mean,

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:10.503
you asked me a question

00:05:10.503 --> 00:05:12.103
so honestly, yeah that was my,

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.720
for some reason opiates to me

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:15.870
made everything right.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:17.811
- And how does heroin compare to pills?

00:05:17.811 --> 00:05:20.199
- (chuckles) Terribly honestly.

00:05:20.199 --> 00:05:21.250
If you want my opinion,

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:24.010
one of the best pills I've
ever had was Oxycontin.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.180
And that gives you like,
a good, like (sighs)

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:32.463
warm confident feeling
but also gives you energy.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:36.297
And for me Oxycontin was the tits, dude.

00:05:36.297 --> 00:05:37.870
It was the only pill I wanted to take.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.260
It was the only drug I wanted to take.

00:05:39.260 --> 00:05:41.550
But they stopped making those things.

00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:44.240
And they got really expensive

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.170
and so the natural progression,

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.910
honestly when I went to my first rehab

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.140
they told me heroin is like,

00:05:50.140 --> 00:05:52.000
so much cheaper and ...

00:05:52.000 --> 00:05:53.420
I never, ever, ever

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:57.180
ever, ever wanted to do heroin like,

00:05:57.180 --> 00:05:58.437
watching movies and stuff like that

00:05:58.437 --> 00:05:59.880
and I'd be honestly I'd be intrigued by it

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.250
but the thought of
sticking a needle in my arm

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:03.850
still to the day is disgusting
as hell to me, dude.

00:06:03.850 --> 00:06:06.560
And it blows my mind
that I even do it, dude.

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:09.779
But being dope-sick is terrible.

00:06:09.779 --> 00:06:11.530
I mean you feel like you're dying.

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:13.360
You honestly feel like you're dying.

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.060
And so I mean, instead
of feeling like dying,

00:06:17.060 --> 00:06:17.893
instead of dying,

00:06:17.893 --> 00:06:18.880
it's like fight or flight.

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.040
I either gonna die or I'm gonna

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:21.113
like get well.

00:06:22.626 --> 00:06:23.800
And you know.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:24.990
I've chosen you know...

00:06:25.953 --> 00:06:26.786
I mean, honestly a few times I've chosen

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:29.370
to rather die and get sober

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:30.820
and I really enjoyed those times.

00:06:30.820 --> 00:06:31.740
But!

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:33.550
Yeah, that's pretty--

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:35.983
I'm not even sure I remember
the exact question, but.

00:06:35.983 --> 00:06:37.530
- Have you been clean before?

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.030
- Yeah the most time
I've had was 17 months.

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:41.820
- And how'd you do it?
- AA.

00:06:43.210 --> 00:06:45.460
I got arrested and I got sent to a program

00:06:46.492 --> 00:06:47.440
where I did six months there.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.400
Actually I got sent to one program

00:06:48.400 --> 00:06:49.460
and I was there for like a week,

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:52.630
I found out my ex-wife (chuckles)
blocked me on Instagram

00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:54.850
and so I got high.

00:06:54.850 --> 00:06:55.683
It was stupid.

00:06:55.683 --> 00:06:56.516
And then I went back to court,

00:06:56.516 --> 00:06:57.610
turn myself in.

00:06:57.610 --> 00:06:59.410
They sent me to another program

00:06:59.410 --> 00:07:00.980
where I did six months.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.837
And actually I was sentenced to six months

00:07:02.837 --> 00:07:04.870
but I ended up doing seven months

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:06.410
and then I did another

00:07:06.410 --> 00:07:08.730
you know, continuous to that 18 months,

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:10.950
17 months sober

00:07:10.950 --> 00:07:12.527
in a sober living

00:07:12.527 --> 00:07:15.810
and I started managing
sober living and all that.

00:07:15.810 --> 00:07:17.523
And I had sponsor and sponsee,

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:19.550
but yeah,

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:21.040
I got uncomfortable.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.940
And stopped going to AA

00:07:22.940 --> 00:07:24.440
and I wound up back over here.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.300
- Does you family know
where you're at today?

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.290
- Yeah.

00:07:30.290 --> 00:07:31.680
- What do they tell you?

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:32.513
- They love me.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.210
Yeah. Trying to be as honest
as possible with them.

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.043
I'm not gonna tell them like,

00:07:37.043 --> 00:07:38.440
the details of everything I'm doing

00:07:38.440 --> 00:07:40.140
because it's just going
to be heartbreaking.

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:40.973
You know?

00:07:40.973 --> 00:07:43.301
But, yeah they generally know what's up.

00:07:43.301 --> 00:07:44.703
- What do you do for money now?

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:46.483
- Honestly,

00:07:47.494 --> 00:07:49.316
(whispering) it's a little illegal.

00:07:49.316 --> 00:07:52.000
- (chuckles) Everything everyone
does down here is illegal.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:53.223
- Mm-hmm at least.

00:07:54.810 --> 00:07:55.980
- So you play music?

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.763
- Yeah I just you know.

00:07:57.763 --> 00:08:00.090
I don't really play anymore
professionally obviously.

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:01.800
- But music helps you
deal with everything?

00:08:01.800 --> 00:08:04.450
- Music is not really an option

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:07.330
it's just music.

00:08:07.330 --> 00:08:09.020
It's like a language.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.500
It's like if I'm gonna speak or think

00:08:11.500 --> 00:08:13.110
or know how I feel about something

00:08:13.110 --> 00:08:16.350
I usually figure out
how that is via music.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:17.950
I guess.

00:08:17.950 --> 00:08:19.150
Yeah music is essential.

00:08:20.180 --> 00:08:22.089
I suck at it now though.

00:08:22.089 --> 00:08:22.922
- What do you think the chances

00:08:22.922 --> 00:08:24.920
are of you getting clean
and off the street?

00:08:26.417 --> 00:08:27.900
- The chances?

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:29.410
Actually they're high.

00:08:29.410 --> 00:08:30.660
Super-duper high.

00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.113
I mean it may seem like
I'm just being like,

00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.800
I don't know

00:08:35.800 --> 00:08:37.750
just hope, wishful thinking or whatever

00:08:38.926 --> 00:08:40.060
but I enjoy being sober a lot.

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:40.893
I really did.

00:08:40.893 --> 00:08:41.726
It's just,

00:08:41.726 --> 00:08:42.670
again I would like to be sober now.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:44.727
I was talking with my buddy earlier

00:08:44.727 --> 00:08:48.129
about it and it's just
the fear of detoxing

00:08:48.129 --> 00:08:48.962
is a pain in the ass, dude.

00:08:48.962 --> 00:08:49.963
It's just not a pain in the ass,

00:08:49.963 --> 00:08:50.910
I feel like I'm dying.

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:53.220
- What do they give you when you detox?

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.440
- Subutex or Suboxone.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:58.860
Just like a pill to you know lower,

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.830
taper down, you know.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:01.663
And there's hope for a little bit

00:09:01.663 --> 00:09:02.530
but then...

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:04.707
It's just that I'm being a wuss, dude.

00:09:04.707 --> 00:09:05.547
I'm being a wuss.

00:09:05.547 --> 00:09:06.630
I know what I need to do.

00:09:06.630 --> 00:09:08.300
I know how to do it even.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:10.543
I'm just postponing
the inevitable I guess.

00:09:12.550 --> 00:09:13.383
Yeah.

00:09:15.907 --> 00:09:16.810
- So do you have kids?

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.510
- Nope, no kids.

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:19.920
I want to have kids.

00:09:19.920 --> 00:09:21.650
Absolutely I don't want to
miss out on that at all.

00:09:21.650 --> 00:09:23.610
At all.

00:09:23.610 --> 00:09:25.583
I love my niece and my nephew so much.

00:09:26.518 --> 00:09:27.818
(voice flutters) Oh sorry.

00:09:29.183 --> 00:09:30.016
- And how old are you?

00:09:30.016 --> 00:09:30.849
- I'm 36.

00:09:32.111 --> 00:09:33.190
But I'm glad I don't have kids now

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.490
because that would just be

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:37.890
I'd be a terrible dad. Yeah.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:40.080
- Well, Rocco, thank you so
